  "worked_solution": "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overset{―}{PR}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $Q$ to the line $\\overset{⟷}{PR},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{PR}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overset{―}{PR}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248996/assets/664c9507be2e02908b8a151d0c58222545a84a7d71648c28e61badfb23e1981b.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $Q$ to $\\overset{⟷}{PR}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248996/assets/89bc576f142925d0ef639e3a2ade1da2900e24f920e2469fe159b6a8eda238c7.png)",
